A||N||3||turbo86se||No spark?||||5
Z||000000||turbo86se||11-03-1999||11:58 AM||||<BR>hey everyone,<BR>The past couple days I've noticed a small problem with my 88 coupe. I'm having trouble starting the engine. It will crank for a couple seconds with no luck of starting before I shut it off. After I wait a couple seconds, and try to restart it, it usually starts right up. The engine has 115,000 miles, runs great when started, doesn't run hot, and doensn't sputter and die when driving.<BR>Any ideas?<BR>Thanks!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||11-03-1999||12:12 PM||||Are you sure there is no spark?  Sounds to me like one possible culprit could be the fuel pump.  Do you hear it click on and off?  Turn the key to the run position, the pump should turn on for a second or two, then off.  If it continuosly runs, or never turns on, there may not be enough pressure at the first cranking session.  It's an easy thing to check first.||||reg||5
Z||000002||theogre||11-03-1999||12:59 PM||||the fuel system take a few sec to pump up even with a perfect pump.<P>turn the key to run but wait about 5 sec before starting. see if that improves things.<P>GM EFI typically cranks 5-12 sec.<P>Replace the fuel filter. if it's blocked it could slow presurizing the system.<P>you should also check fuel pressure. if the regulator is leaking slightly it will also mess with starting. might not be leaking enough to mess up when running.||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||11-03-1999||02:01 PM||||thanks for the advice, fiero56, theogre! I just replaced the fuel pump last week, and I can hear the pump turn on when I turn the key to the on positon. It must be the fuel filter, it's been on there close to a year. I should have replaced it when my mechanic told me to! Thanks again guys! ||||reg||1
